@startuml 01 - Cadastro e Consentimento
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

actor Usuário as U
participant "WhatsApp\n(Meta)" as WA
participant "Nginx\n(Ingress)" as NG
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Kafka\nmessages.inbound" as K1
participant "Chat Service" as CS
participant "PostgreSQL" as PG
participant "Kafka\naudit.log" as KA
participant "Kafka\nmessages.outbound" as K2
participant "Outbound Worker" as OW
participant "Pluggy\n(Open Finance)" as PL

U -> WA : Envia primeira mensagem
WA -> NG : POST /webhook (HMAC-SHA256)
NG -> GW : Valida assinatura HMAC
GW -> K1 : Produz evento messages.inbound\n(payload criptografado AES-256-GCM)
GW --> WA : HTTP 200 (ack imediato)

K1 -> CS : Consome evento
CS -> PG : SELECT por phone_number_hash\n(HMAC-SHA256 do número)
PG --> CS : 0 resultados (usuário não existe)

CS -> K2 : Produz WhatsApp Flow\nde onboarding (nome, senha 6 dígitos,\nconfirmação de senha, aceite LGPD,\npolítica de privacidade)
K2 -> OW : Consome evento
OW -> WA : Envia Flow via Meta Cloud API
WA -> U : Exibe formulário de cadastro

U -> WA : Preenche nome, cria senha de 6 dígitos\ne aceita termos
WA -> NG : POST /webhook
NG -> GW : Valida HMAC
GW -> K1 : Produz evento (dados do formulário criptografados)
GW --> WA : HTTP 200

K1 -> CS : Consome evento
CS -> CS : Gera bcrypt(pin, saltRounds: 12)
CS -> PG : INSERT users\n(name_encrypted, phone_number_hash,\npin_hash, data_retention_consent=true,\nprivacy_accepted_at=NOW())
PG --> CS : user_id gerado

CS -> KA : Produz audit.log\n(operation: consent_granted,\nuser_id, timestamp)

CS -> K2 : Produz link Pluggy Connect Widget\npara vinculação Open Finance
K2 -> OW : Consome evento
OW -> WA : Envia link ao usuário
WA -> U : Exibe link do Pluggy

U -> PL : Acessa Pluggy Connect Widget\ne autoriza compartilhamento bancário
PL -> GW : Webhook item_id (consentimento ativo)
GW -> K1 : Produz user.events\n(tipo: pluggy_consent_granted)

K1 -> CS : Consome evento
CS -> PG : INSERT consents\n(user_id, pluggy_item_id, scope[],\nstatus=active, expires_at=+12meses)
PG --> CS : consent_id gerado

CS -> KA : Produz audit.log\n(operation: pluggy_consent_granted)
CS -> K2 : Produz mensagem de boas-vindas
K2 -> OW : Consome evento
OW -> WA : Envia confirmação ao usuário
WA -> U : "Conta vinculada! Posso começar\na analisar suas finanças."
@enduml
